WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.606
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:05.906 --> 00:00:09.129
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:16.285
Unit twenty-one: Modal Nuances of Probability. Today you will grade predictions from uncertain to certain.

4
00:00:16.585 --> 00:00:19.225
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:23.202
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:25.005
Be bound to.

7
00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:28.411
Be bound to means almost certain to happen.

8
00:00:29.017 --> 00:00:30.262
He is bound to win.

9
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.781
Your turn. Say: Be bound to.

10
00:00:36.633 --> 00:00:37.936
Be bound to.

11
00:00:38.683 --> 00:00:39.928
Be likely to.

12
00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:42.847
Be likely to means probable.

13
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:44.811
It is likely to rain.

14
00:00:45.417 --> 00:00:48.394
Your turn. Say: Be likely to.

15
00:00:51.233 --> 00:00:52.548
Be likely to.

16
00:00:53.283 --> 00:00:54.482
Be sure to.

17
00:00:55.483 --> 00:00:57.622
Be sure to means certain to happen.

18
00:00:58.217 --> 00:00:59.682
She is sure to agree.

19
00:01:00.283 --> 00:01:03.133
Your turn. Say: Be sure to.

20
00:01:05.967 --> 00:01:07.107
Be sure to.

21
00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.223
Be unlikely to.

22
00:01:10.217 --> 00:01:12.599
Be unlikely to means not probable.

23
00:01:13.183 --> 00:01:14.742
He is unlikely to come.

24
00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:18.211
Your turn. Say: Be unlikely to.

25
00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:22.335
Be unlikely to.

26
00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.050
May well.

27
00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:26.933
May well means quite possibly.

28
00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:28.772
It may well rain.

29
00:01:29.383 --> 00:01:31.885
Your turn. Say: May well.

30
00:01:34.733 --> 00:01:35.943
May well.

31
00:01:36.683 --> 00:01:37.533
Could well.

32
00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.584
Could well means quite possibly.

33
00:01:41.183 --> 00:01:42.568
She could well be right.

34
00:01:43.183 --> 00:01:45.685
Your turn. Say: Could well.

35
00:01:48.533 --> 00:01:49.442
Could well.

36
00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:51.277
Probability.

37
00:01:52.283 --> 00:01:54.910
Probability means how likely something is.

38
00:01:55.517 --> 00:01:57.330
The probability is high.

39
00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.499
Your turn. Say: Probability.

40
00:02:03.333 --> 00:02:04.451
Probability.

41
00:02:05.217 --> 00:02:06.253
Certainty.

42
00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.551
Certainty means being completely sure.

43
00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:11.952
A certainty of success.

44
00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:14.970
Your turn. Say: Certainty.

45
00:02:17.833 --> 00:02:18.927
Certainty.

46
00:02:19.733 --> 00:02:23.361
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.217 --> 00:02:27.888
Visal, which is stronger: He is bound to win, or He may well win?

48
00:02:28.983 --> 00:02:39.530
He is bound to win. Be bound to and be sure to express near-certainty, while may well and could well express a good possibility but not certainty.

49
00:02:40.617 --> 00:02:42.198
What about the lower end?

50
00:02:43.283 --> 00:02:53.064
Be unlikely to and might not show low probability: He is unlikely to come. Between them, be likely to means more than 50 percent.

51
00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.859
Where do these fit on a scale?

52
00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:13.581
From highest to lowest: be bound to, be sure to, be likely to, may well, could well, might, be unlikely to. Choose the one that matches your confidence, especially in forecasts and academic hedging.

53
00:03:14.733 --> 00:03:16.466
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:17.317 --> 00:03:25.400
Grammar focus: Probability: subject plus be bound and likely and sure and unlikely to plus verb; modal plus well.

55
00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:26.863
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:29.317
He is bound to win the race.

57
00:03:30.217 --> 00:03:32.100
It may well rain this afternoon.

58
00:03:33.017 --> 00:03:35.214
She is unlikely to arrive early.

59
00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:44.246
Bound to and sure to are nearly certain. Likely to is probable. May well and could well are quite possible. Unlikely to is improbable.

60
00:03:44.983 --> 00:03:48.170
Be careful! Don't say: He is bound win.

61
00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:52.005
Say: He is bound to win.

62
00:03:52.305 --> 00:03:53.666
Use to after bound.

63
00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.887
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:59.316
Forecasting the Future.

65
00:03:59.616 --> 00:04:02.568
The team is bound to win after such a strong season.

66
00:04:03.567 --> 00:04:05.427
It is likely to rain by evening.

67
00:04:06.433 --> 00:04:08.549
The weather could well change tomorrow.

68
00:04:09.533 --> 00:04:12.218
The coach is unlikely to make any changes.

69
00:04:13.233 --> 00:04:15.755
Each phrase gives a different level of certainty.

70
00:04:16.867 --> 00:04:21.019
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:21.883 --> 00:04:24.396
He blank to win. (almost certain)

72
00:04:24.696 --> 00:04:28.361
A, is bound. B, may well. C, is unlikely.

73
00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.097
The answer is A: is bound.

74
00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.959
It blank well rain tonight.

75
00:04:37.259 --> 00:04:40.739
A, may. B, is. C, has.

76
00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.218
The answer is A: may.

77
00:04:47.383 --> 00:04:49.232
Which is the weakest probability?

78
00:04:49.532 --> 00:04:53.882
A, is bound to. B, is likely to. C, is unlikely to.

79
00:04:57.433 --> 00:05:00.106
The answer is C: is unlikely to.

80
00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:03.168
Be sure to expresses blank.

81
00:05:03.468 --> 00:05:07.842
A, near certainty. B, impossibility. C, a request.

82
00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.026
The answer is A: near certainty.

83
00:05:15.183 --> 00:05:18.379
According to the reading, who is unlikely to make changes?

84
00:05:18.679 --> 00:05:22.506
A, the coach. B, the player. C, the referee.

85
00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:28.182
The answer is A: the coach.

86
00:05:29.367 --> 00:05:32.425
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:33.283 --> 00:05:36.328
Make three predictions with different levels of certainty.

88
00:05:45.117 --> 00:05:46.687
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:46.987 --> 00:05:56.157
The sun is bound to rise tomorrow. It is likely to be hot this afternoon. It could well rain in the evening. I use different phrases to show how sure I am.

90
00:05:56.457 --> 00:05:58.190
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:59.083 --> 00:06:08.295
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and probability: subject plus be bound and likely and sure and unlikely to plus verb; modal plus well.

92
00:06:08.595 --> 00:06:13.523
Today's value is rational reflection. Pause to think carefully before you decide.

93
00:06:13.823 --> 00:06:16.580
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:19.683
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

